IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 21 (COSTS), rule 10 (fixed costs) and APPENDIX 1 (fixed costs), Parts 1 to 6.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Rules 1 to 9 and 11 to 16 are in roc5-o21-general.l4 and rules 17 to 29 in roc5-o21-assessment.l4.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- The converter flattened the Appendix's tables into one cell per line: the three court columns
-- (High Court, District Court, Magistrate's Court) follow each row in that order, and the quotes below are
-- those cells as they stand.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc5-o20.l4.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text's own yes and no;
-- NOTHING is "not covered"; a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A SUM of money is an `o 21 app 1 allowance`, because the Appendix gives fixed sums, ranges, "up to" additions
-- and "actual" amounts.  A sum cannot carry a "no", so each paragraph that can say no has a yes/no twin that
-- answers JUST FALSE where the text says the item is not allowed, and the sum function answers NOTHING there.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 21, rule 10 and Appendix 1 -- fixed costs`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:3001 | 10. In the cases to which Appendix 1 to this Order applies, the amount of costs allowed are as set out in that Appendix, unless the Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 21 r 10 (src:3001-3001)
GIVEN `the case is one to which Appendix 1 to this Order applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 10 the amount of costs allowed is the amount set out in Appendix 1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the case is one to which Appendix 1 to this Order applies`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the cases to which Appendix 1 to this Order applies"
        IF `the Court has otherwise ordered`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The three columns of every table in the Appendix, named as the text names them.
DECLARE `o 21 app 1 court column` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 app 1 the High Court`
    `o 21 app 1 a District Court`
    `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court`

-- What a table cell can say.  "Add up to $1,000" is an addition and not a sum; "Actual fees", "Actual cost",
-- "Actual GST payable" and "Actual amount allowed" are the amounts as incurred; "$350 plus disbursement" is a
-- sum together with the disbursements that the paragraph allows.
DECLARE `o 21 app 1 allowance` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` HAS `the sum` IS A NUMBER
    `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum plus disbursement` HAS `the sum` IS A NUMBER
    `o 21 app 1 a range` HAS `the lowest sum` IS A NUMBER, `the highest sum` IS A NUMBER
    `o 21 app 1 an addition of up to` HAS `the most` IS A NUMBER
    `o 21 app 1 the actual fees`
    `o 21 app 1 the actual cost`
    `o 21 app 1 the actual GST payable`
    `o 21 app 1 the actual amount allowed`
    `o 21 app 1 the charges, commission, expenses and fees paid to the Sheriff`
    `o 21 app 1 the reasonable disbursements incurred by the applicant`

-- The Appendix's "High Court" column is read as the General Division when a case is stated by the court that
-- hears it (assumed, not ruled: the text of the Rules defines "General Division" as the General Division of the
-- High Court and never says the column is that Division).  Other levels have no column.
GIVEN level IS A `Court level`
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 21 app 1 court column`
`o 21 app 1 the column for the court level` MEANS
    CONSIDER level
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST `o 21 app 1 the High Court`
    WHEN `District Court` THEN JUST `o 21 app 1 a District Court`
    WHEN `Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Appendix's tables have a High Court, a District Court and a Magistrate's Court column and no other

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Part 1 -- costs on judgment without trial (paragraph 1)`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 21 app 1 para 1(1) case` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(a) the defendant pays the amount claimed within the time and in the manner required by the endorsement of the originating claim`
    `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(b) the claimant obtains final judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence`
    `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(i) the claimant obtains final judgment under Order 9, Rule 17 unconditionally`
    `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(ii) the Court dismisses an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17`
    `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(iii) the Court gives the defendant unconditional permission to defend an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17`
    `o 21 app 1 para 1 another case`

-- (1) and (2): the Part 2 scale applies to the listed cases; (2) takes Part 1 away where the claimant is also
-- entitled to damages to be assessed or claims relief of the nature in Order 52 rule 1 (a seam: Order 52 is
-- another part's).
-- src:3138 | 1.— (1) The scale of costs set out in Part 2 of this Appendix applies in relation to the following cases: ( a )
-- src:3139 | cases in which the defendant pays the amount claimed within the time and in the manner required by the endorsement of the originating claim;
-- src:3140 | ( b )
-- src:3141 | cases in which the claimant obtains final judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence;
-- src:3142 | ( c )
-- src:3143 | cases in which — (i)
-- src:3144 | the claimant obtains final judgment under Order 9, Rule 17 unconditionally;
-- src:3145 | (ii)
-- src:3146 | the Court dismisses an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17; or
-- src:3147 | (iii)
-- src:3148 | the Court gives the defendant against whom an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17 is made unconditional permission to defend.
-- src:3149 | (2) Where the claimant is also entitled under the judgment to damages to be assessed, or where the claimant claims any relief of the nature specified in Order 52, Rule 1, this Part does not apply.
@ref O 21 app 1 para 1 (src:3138-3149)
GIVEN case IS A `o 21 app 1 para 1(1) case`
      `the claimant is also entitled under the judgment to damages to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 52 r 1 the claimant claims relief of the nature specified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 app 1 para 1(1) the scale of costs in Part 2 applies to the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant is also entitled under the judgment to damages to be assessed` OR `o 52 r 1 the claimant claims relief of the nature specified` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this Part does not apply" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF `o 52 r 1 the claimant claims relief of the nature specified` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the relief is "of the nature specified in Order 52, Rule 1" is Order 52 rule 1's answer
        IF case EQUALS `o 21 app 1 para 1 another case`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "applies in relation to the following cases" and the text does not say the scale is not used elsewhere
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3): for the cases in (1)(a) and (b) where the claimant is entitled to indemnity costs, Parts 2 and 3 both apply.
-- src:3150 | (3) In respect of the cases set out in sub‑paragraph (1)( a ) and ( b ), where the claimant is entitled under the judgment to costs on an indemnity basis, the scale of costs and disbursements set out in both Parts 2 and 3 of this Appendix apply.
@ref O 21 app 1 para 1(3) (src:3150-3150)
GIVEN case IS A `o 21 app 1 para 1(1) case`
      `the claimant is entitled under the judgment to costs on an indemnity basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 app 1 para 1(3) the scale of costs and disbursements in both Parts 2 and 3 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF case EQUALS `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(i) the claimant obtains final judgment under Order 9, Rule 17 unconditionally`
           OR case EQUALS `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(ii) the Court dismisses an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17`
           OR case EQUALS `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(iii) the Court gives the defendant unconditional permission to defend an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17`
           OR case EQUALS `o 21 app 1 para 1 another case`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In respect of the cases set out in sub‑paragraph (1)( a ) and ( b )"
        IF NOT `the claimant is entitled under the judgment to costs on an indemnity basis`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the claimant is entitled under the judgment to costs on an indemnity basis" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Part 2 -- basic costs (paragraphs 2 and 3)`
-- ===========================================================================

-- Paragraph 2: the basic costs, by sub-paragraph of paragraph 1(1) and by court.
-- src:3153 | 2. Costs to be allowed (excluding disbursements) in cases under the following sub-paragraphs of paragraph 1(1) in Part 1 of this Appendix:
-- src:3154 | High Court
-- src:3155 | District Court
-- src:3156 | Magistrate ’ s Court
-- src:3157 | ( a )
-- src:3158 | under sub-paragraph ( a )
-- src:3159 | $2,000
-- src:3160 | $1,500
-- src:3161 | $800
-- src:3162 | ( b )
-- src:3163 | under sub-paragraph ( b )
-- src:3164 | $2,300
-- src:3165 | $1,800
-- src:3166 | $1,000
-- src:3167 | ( c )
-- src:3168 | under sub-paragraph ( c )
-- src:3169 | $4,000 to $15,000
-- src:3170 | $3,000 to $10,000
-- src:3171 | $2,000 to $6,000
@ref O 21 app 1 para 2 (src:3153-3171)
GIVEN case IS A `o 21 app 1 para 1(1) case`
      court IS A `o 21 app 1 court column`
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 21 app 1 allowance`
`o 21 app 1 para 2 the costs to be allowed excluding disbursements` MEANS
    CONSIDER case
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(a) the defendant pays the amount claimed within the time and in the manner required by the endorsement of the originating claim` THEN
        CONSIDER court
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 the High Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 2000)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a District Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 1500)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 800)
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(b) the claimant obtains final judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` THEN
        CONSIDER court
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 the High Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 2300)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a District Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 1800)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 1000)
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(i) the claimant obtains final judgment under Order 9, Rule 17 unconditionally` THEN
        CONSIDER court
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 the High Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 4000 15000)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a District Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 3000 10000)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 2000 6000)
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(ii) the Court dismisses an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17` THEN
        CONSIDER court
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 the High Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 4000 15000)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a District Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 3000 10000)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 2000 6000)
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 1(1)(c)(iii) the Court gives the defendant unconditional permission to defend an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17` THEN
        CONSIDER court
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 the High Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 4000 15000)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a District Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 3000 10000)
        WHEN `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` 2000 6000)
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 1 another case` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in cases under the following sub-paragraphs of paragraph 1(1) in Part 1 of this Appendix"

-- Paragraph 3(1): each additional defendant served.
-- src:3172 | COSTS FOR ADDITIONAL ITEMS
-- src:3173 | Costs to be allowed
-- src:3174 | High Court
-- src:3175 | District Court
-- src:3176 | Magistrate’s Court
-- src:3177 | 3.—(1) Where there is more than one defendant, in respect of each additional defendant served —
-- src:3178 | ( a )
-- src:3179 | if the additional defendant is represented by the same solicitor as any other defendant
-- src:3180 | $100
-- src:3181 | $100
-- src:3182 | $100
-- src:3183 | ( b )
-- src:3184 | in any other case
-- src:3185 | $200
-- src:3186 | $200
-- src:3187 | $150
@ref O 21 app 1 para 3(1) (src:3172-3187)
GIVEN court IS A `o 21 app 1 court column`
      `there is more than one defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional defendant is represented by the same solicitor as any other defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 21 app 1 allowance`
`o 21 app 1 para 3(1) the costs for each additional defendant served` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is more than one defendant`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a sum cannot carry the no): the yes/no twin answers JUST FALSE where there is only one defendant
        IF `the additional defendant is represented by the same solicitor as any other defendant`
        THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 100)
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER court
                  WHEN `o 21 app 1 the High Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 200)
                  WHEN `o 21 app 1 a District Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 200)
                  WHEN `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 150)

-- src:3177 | 3.—(1) Where there is more than one defendant, in respect of each additional defendant served —
-- src:3178 | ( a )
-- src:3179 | if the additional defendant is represented by the same solicitor as any other defendant
-- src:3180 | $100
-- src:3181 | $100
-- src:3182 | $100
-- src:3183 | ( b )
-- src:3184 | in any other case
-- src:3185 | $200
-- src:3186 | $200
-- src:3187 | $150
@ref O 21 app 1 para 3(1) (src:3177-3187)
GIVEN `there is more than one defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional defendant has been served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 app 1 para 3(1) costs are allowed for the additional defendant` MEANS
    IF `there is more than one defendant` AND `the additional defendant has been served`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is more than one defendant, in respect of each additional defendant served" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]

-- Paragraph 3(2): substituted service.
-- src:3188 | (2) Where substituted service is ordered and effected, in respect of each defendant served
-- src:3189 | $350 plus disbursement
-- src:3190 | $350 plus disbursement
-- src:3191 | $300 plus disbursement
@ref O 21 app 1 para 3(2) (src:3188-3191)
GIVEN court IS A `o 21 app 1 court column`
GIVETH A `o 21 app 1 allowance`
`o 21 app 1 para 3(2) the costs for each defendant served by substituted service` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 the High Court` THEN `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum plus disbursement` 350
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 a District Court` THEN `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum plus disbursement` 350
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court` THEN `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum plus disbursement` 300

-- src:3188 | (2) Where substituted service is ordered and effected, in respect of each defendant served
@ref O 21 app 1 para 3(2) (src:3188-3188)
GIVEN `substituted service is ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `substituted service is effected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 app 1 para 3(2) costs are allowed for substituted service` MEANS
    IF `substituted service is ordered` AND `substituted service is effected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where substituted service is ordered and effected" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]

-- Paragraph 3(3): service out of Singapore.
