      `service out of Singapore is effected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 app 1 para 3(3) costs are allowed for service out of Singapore` MEANS
    IF `service out of Singapore is ordered` AND `service out of Singapore is effected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where service out of Singapore is ordered and effected" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]

-- The disbursements allowed under (2) and (3): the same in all three columns.
DECLARE `o 21 app 1 para 3(3) disbursement` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(3)(a) court fees`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(3)(b) affirmation fees for affidavit in support of application`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(3)(c) each attempted service`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(3)(d)(i) substituted service within Singapore by posting on the door`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(3)(d)(ii) substituted service within Singapore by advertisement`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(3)(e) service out of Singapore`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(3)(f) title searches`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3 another disbursement`

