-- Paragraph 3(4): an affidavit of service for a judgment in default.
DECLARE `o 21 app 1 para 3(4) kind of judgment` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(4) judgment in default of defence`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(4) judgment pursuant to an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17`
    `o 21 app 1 para 3(4) another kind of judgment`

-- src:3238 | (4) In the case of a judgment in default of defence or judgment pursuant to an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17, where notice of intention to contest or not contest is not given on the day on which the notice is filed, and the claimant makes an affidavit of service for the purpose of a judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest (the allowance to include the search fee)
-- src:3239 | $200
-- src:3240 | $200
-- src:3241 | $150
@ref O 21 app 1 para 3(4) (src:3238-3241)
GIVEN court IS A `o 21 app 1 court column`
      kind IS A `o 21 app 1 para 3(4) kind of judgment`
      `notice of intention to contest or not contest is not given on the day on which the notice is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant makes an affidavit of service for the purpose of a judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 21 app 1 allowance`
`o 21 app 1 para 3(4) the costs for the affidavit of service, including the search fee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `o 21 app 1 para 3(4) another kind of judgment`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a judgment in default of defence or judgment pursuant to an application for summary judgment under Order 9, Rule 17"
        IF NOT (`notice of intention to contest or not contest is not given on the day on which the notice is filed` AND `the claimant makes an affidavit of service for the purpose of a judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a sum cannot carry the no): the yes/no twin answers JUST FALSE where the conditions are not met
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER court
                  WHEN `o 21 app 1 the High Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 200)
                  WHEN `o 21 app 1 a District Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 200)
                  WHEN `o 21 app 1 a Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 150)

