@ref O 21 app 1 para 8(2) (src:3340-3340)
GIVEN `the action is a non-injury motor accident action` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the action is filed in the Magistrates' Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 app 1 para 8(2) the scale of costs in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b), together with paragraph 3 in Part 2, applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is a non-injury motor accident action` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the action is a non-injury motor accident action is not known
        IF `the action is a non-injury motor accident action` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the action is filed in the Magistrates' Courts`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to all non‑injury motor accident actions filed in the Magistrates’ Courts"

DECLARE `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) stage` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) any stage before defence is served`
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) where defence is served`
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) where defence to counterclaim is served`
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) where affidavits of evidence-in-chief are exchanged`
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) the 1st day of trial`
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) each subsequent day of trial`

-- The table: liability and quantum concluded together.  The three sum columns are: less than $1,000; $1,000 to
-- less than $10,000; $10,000 and above.
-- src:3340 | 8.— (1) In this Part, “non‑injury motor accident action” means an action arising out of an accident on land due to a collision or an apprehended collision involving one or more motor vehicles, but not involving any claim for personal injuries. (2) The scale of costs set out in sub‑paragraphs ( a ) and ( b ) (which are exclusive of disbursements) together with paragraph 3 in Part 2 of this Appendix apply to all non‑injury motor accident actions filed in the Magistrates’ Courts — ( a )
-- src:3341 | where the matter is concluded in respect of the issues of liability and quantum simultaneously, the costs are to follow the TABLE below:
-- src:3342 | TABLE
-- src:3343 | Stage of proceedings matter is concluded
-- src:3344 | Sum settled or awarded (excluding interest if any)
-- src:3345 | Less than $1,000
-- src:3346 | $1,000 to less than $10,000
-- src:3347 | $10,000 and above
-- src:3348 | Any stage before defence is served
-- src:3349 | $1,000
-- src:3350 | $1,000 — $1,200
-- src:3351 | $1,200 — $1,500
-- src:3352 | Where defence is served
-- src:3353 | $1,000
-- src:3354 | $1,200 — $1,500
-- src:3355 | $1,500 — $1,800
-- src:3356 | Where defence to counterclaim is served
-- src:3357 | $1,000
-- src:3358 | $1,500 — $1,800
-- src:3359 | $1,800 — $2,100
-- src:3360 | Where affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief are exchanged
-- src:3361 | $1,300
-- src:3362 | $1,800 — $2,800
-- src:3363 | $2,300 — $3,500
-- src:3364 | The 1st day of trial
-- src:3365 | $1,500 — $2,000
-- src:3366 | $3,200 — $3,800
-- src:3367 | $3,800 — $6,000
-- src:3368 | Each subsequent day of trial
-- src:3369 | Add up to $1,000
-- src:3370 | Add up to $1,500
-- src:3371 | Add up to $3,000
@ref O 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) (src:3340-3371)
GIVEN stage IS A `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) stage`
      `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `o 21 app 1 allowance`
`o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) the costs for the stage and the sum` MEANS
    CONSIDER stage
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) any stage before defence is served` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 1000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 1000
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 10000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a range` 1000 1200
            OTHERWISE `o 21 app 1 a range` 1200 1500
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) where defence is served` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 1000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 1000
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 10000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a range` 1200 1500
            OTHERWISE `o 21 app 1 a range` 1500 1800
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) where defence to counterclaim is served` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 1000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 1000
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 10000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a range` 1500 1800
            OTHERWISE `o 21 app 1 a range` 1800 2100
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) where affidavits of evidence-in-chief are exchanged` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 1000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` 1300
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 10000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a range` 1800 2800
            OTHERWISE `o 21 app 1 a range` 2300 3500
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) the 1st day of trial` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 1000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a range` 1500 2000
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 10000 THEN `o 21 app 1 a range` 3200 3800
            OTHERWISE `o 21 app 1 a range` 3800 6000
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(a) each subsequent day of trial` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 1000 THEN `o 21 app 1 an addition of up to` 1000
            IF `the sum settled or awarded, excluding interest if any` LESS THAN 10000 THEN `o 21 app 1 an addition of up to` 1500
            OTHERWISE `o 21 app 1 an addition of up to` 3000

DECLARE `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b) when liability is resolved` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b)(i) before the originating claim is issued`
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b)(ii) after the originating claim is issued but before affidavits of evidence-in-chief are exchanged`
    `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b)(iii) after affidavits of evidence-in-chief are exchanged`

-- (b): liability and quantum resolved separately: costs are a percentage of the scale in the table.
-- src:3372 | ( b )
-- src:3373 | where liability and quantum are resolved separately (i.e., interlocutory judgment is entered with damages to be assessed), costs will be fixed at a percentage of the scale in the TABLE as follows, depending on the stage at which liability and quantum are resolved: (i)
-- src:3374 | if liability is resolved before the originating claim is issued and the claimant follows or ought to have followed the procedure in these Rules or the relevant practice direction, costs will be 80% of the scale at the relevant stage at which the matter is concluded;
-- src:3375 | (ii)
-- src:3376 | if liability is resolved after the originating claim is issued but before affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief are exchanged, costs will be 90% of the scale;
-- src:3377 | (iii)
-- src:3378 | if liability is resolved after affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief are exchanged, costs will be 100% of the scale.
@ref O 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b) (src:3372-3378)
GIVEN timing IS A `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b) when liability is resolved`
      `the claimant follows or ought to have followed the procedure in these Rules or the relevant practice direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b) the percentage of the scale` MEANS
    CONSIDER timing
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b)(i) before the originating claim is issued` THEN
        IF `the claimant follows or ought to have followed the procedure in these Rules or the relevant practice direction`
        THEN JUST (80%)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and the claimant follows or ought to have followed the procedure in these Rules or the relevant practice direction"
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b)(ii) after the originating claim is issued but before affidavits of evidence-in-chief are exchanged` THEN JUST (90%)
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b)(iii) after affidavits of evidence-in-chief are exchanged` THEN JUST (100%)

-- src:3372 | ( b )
-- src:3373 | where liability and quantum are resolved separately (i.e., interlocutory judgment is entered with damages to be assessed), costs will be fixed at a percentage of the scale in the TABLE as follows, depending on the stage at which liability and quantum are resolved: (i)
-- src:3374 | if liability is resolved before the originating claim is issued and the claimant follows or ought to have followed the procedure in these Rules or the relevant practice direction, costs will be 80% of the scale at the relevant stage at which the matter is concluded;
-- src:3375 | (ii)
-- src:3376 | if liability is resolved after the originating claim is issued but before affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief are exchanged, costs will be 90% of the scale;
-- src:3377 | (iii)
-- src:3378 | if liability is resolved after affidavits of evidence‑in‑chief are exchanged, costs will be 100% of the scale.
@ref O 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b) (src:3372-3378)
GIVEN allowance IS AN `o 21 app 1 allowance`
      percentage IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 21 app 1 allowance`
`o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b) the allowance at the percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER allowance
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` sum THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a fixed sum` (sum TIMES percentage))
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 a range` lowest highest THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 a range` (lowest TIMES percentage) (highest TIMES percentage))
    WHEN `o 21 app 1 an addition of up to` most THEN JUST (`o 21 app 1 an addition of up to` (most TIMES percentage))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the percentage is of "the scale in the TABLE" and the TABLE's cells are sums, ranges and additions

-- src:3372 | ( b )
@ref O 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b) (src:3372-3372)
GIVEN `liability and quantum are resolved separately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `interlocutory judgment is entered with damages to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 app 1 para 8(2)(b) costs are fixed at a percentage of the scale in the TABLE` MEANS
    IF `liability and quantum are resolved separately` AND `interlocutory judgment is entered with damages to be assessed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where liability and quantum are resolved separately (i.e., interlocutory judgment is entered with damages to be assessed)" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
